            "result_text": "Perfect! I've successfully created `/app/filter.py`. The script is complete and tested.\n\n## What the script does:\n\nThe filter removes JavaScript from HTML files to prevent XSS attacks by:\n\n1. **Removing script tags** - Eliminates all `<script>` tags and their content\n2. **Removing event handlers** - Strips out attributes like `onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, `onmouseover`, etc.\n3. **Removing JavaScript URLs** - Removes `javascript:` URLs from attributes like `href`, `src`, `action`, `data`, `formaction`, and `poster`\n\n## Key features:\n\n✓ Preserves all legitimate HTML structure (tables, headers, divs, etc.)  \n✓ Preserves safe attributes (`id`, `class`, `data-*`, `style`, `placeholder`, etc.)  \n✓ Preserves formatting and whitespace exactly  \n✓ Handles quoted, single-quoted, and unquoted attribute values  \n✓ Modifies files in-place as requested  \n✓ Provides usage error messages when arguments are missing  \n\n## Usage:\n\n```bash\npython filter.py <html_file>\n```\n\nThe script has been tested against multiple XSS vectors and correctly sanitizes dangerous content while preserving everything else."
